  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian disarmament, protection of civilians and development 2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2021 assessed contributions for international meeting costs, voluntary contributions to sponsorship programs and secretariats of multilateral humanitarian disarmament conventions (mentioned below), and other initiatives to coordinate and implement survey and clearance and victim assistance activities in developing countries contaminated by anti-personnelmines, cluster muntiions and other explosive remnants of war which impede social and economic development.

1. The Ottawa Convention / The Anti-Personnel Mine Ban Treaty.
2. The Convention on Cluster Munitions (CCM)
3. The Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons or CCW / The Inhumane Weapons Convention.
4. The Arms Trade Treaty (ATT)</narrative>
  </description>
